["ItemText"] = {
["GameObject-466230"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG ONE\r\n\r\nDornogal. It feels like I know this place, but I'm experiencing it for the first time. I don't quite understand it. \r\n\r\nI've talked to many of my kin, and they've explained as much as they could, but it hasn't helped at all. \r\n\r\nThis is my home, but it doesn't feel that way. \r\n\r\nI wonder if it ever will.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG TWO\r\n\r\nAs the days go by, attitudes seem to be changing. My kin can be rigid and stubborn, but there's a warmth to them.\r\n\r\nI've learned about what led to my day of awakening. Tribulations that lasted millennia.  \r\n\r\nI've awoken during a shifting age. I wonder what this means for me. Where is my place?",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG THREE\r\n\r\nSpeaker Brinthe insists I come up with a name for myself. I've toyed with different names. \r\n\r\nAurora? It doesn't quite fit, but it's what I saw before I woke.  I will never forget that beautiful light, the warmth of that voice.  \r\n\r\nMaybe something vibrant like Coral?\r\n\r\nNo, that doesn't quite fit either. I'll keep thinking.",
},
{
["Page"] = 4,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG SIX\r\n\r\nI feel less hesitant now. Adjusting to our society and all the rules has proven difficult. \r\n\r\nAs much as I love my kin, I still can't quite understand their adherence to tradition. They say it's what you're supposed to do. \r\n\r\nWhy? \r\n\r\nWhen I asked Brinthe, she had a different answer. At one point we served the Titans. \r\n\r\nBut now? \r\n\r\nNow we choose to serve one another. This has inspired me.",
},
{
["Page"] = 5,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG NINE \r\n\r\nMy name is Dawn. \r\n\r\nI had to write this down. It came to me after watching the sun rise over Dornogal.\r\n\r\nDawn, the start of a new day, of a new age. The end of darkness, the beginning of something more. \r\n\r\nThis I feel represents who I wish to be.",
},
{
["Page"] = 6,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG TEN\r\n\r\nI've been helping the Foreman quite a bit. He has been teaching about the rigid processes that my kin used to experience. \r\n\r\nThe machines don't seem to do well with we Awakened. \r\n\r\nAnd the Foreman's language at times can be harsh. I know he doesn't mean it in that way. \r\n\r\nThank the cogs that Caretakers exist. They seem to be a bit more prepared. \r\n\r\nIt takes time to change your ways--but I hope the Foreman adjusts sooner rather than later.",
},
{
["Page"] = 7,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG TWELVE\r\n\r\nNext week I start implementing my improvements to the Awakening Protocol.\r\n\r\nI hope that they go well. Our awakening shouldn't be frightening. It should feel the same as the song's warm embrace. \r\n\r\nNo matter what happens, I do know this is a step into a new age. \r\n\r\nOne day earthen will travel beyond the shores of Khaz Algar. But for now, the first step.  \r\n\r\nOur society is changing. But there's no reason it must all be at once.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Navigations of the Soul",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 466230,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-526903"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<Light catches glittering script scrawled across the marble walls. Each of the countless names enchanted on the wall sports a different handwriting, from elegant lettering befitting a Magister's thesis spellbook cover to blocky script belaying a child's lack of learning. Some slanted in anger or looped in sorrow.>\r\n\r\nIn honor of those whose blood was shed to secure the survival of our people.\r\n\r\nThough the Eternal Sun may set on our darkest day.\r\n\r\nIt rises again with the coming of the dawn.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Memorial Plaque",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 526903,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-620321"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Patience! Cleverness!\r\n\r\nThose who follow Halazzi have both.\r\n\r\nHalazzi--the silver lynx that stalks the night, waiting hides from all sight.\r\n\r\nHe is called by many names!\r\n\r\nLong Ear\r\n\r\nThe Silver Shadow\r\n\r\nThe Schemer\r\n\r\nThe Night Hunter\r\n\r\nThe Witherbark call upon Halazzi to hide them from their prey, to help them outwit their enemies, to protect them in the night, and to increase their grace in dance and in combat. He brings the mist and rain keeping plants and animals of the forest fit for the hunt. His ears and eyes like the moon pierce the veil revealing lies, mysteries, motivations and the unseen. Praise the playful lynx loa of games, of the moon, of shadow, of the forest, and the HUNT!",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tablet of Halazzi",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 620321,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-191034"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "King Greymane,\r\n\r\nThe ally you sent to aid us was most effective, and in return for your patience, I offer welcome news.\r\n\r\nWith the formation of the new Desolate Council, one of the first topics I propose is the withdrawal of Forsaken troops from the kingdom of Gilneas. In time I hope that we may come closer to agreement, and see both lands into a brighter future.\r\n\r\nWarm Regards,\r\n\r\nCalia Menethil\r\n<The Pallid Lady>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Letter to Greymane",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 191034,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-618571"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<The Shadowgraft hums. It calls to you with the promise of power.\r\n\r\nYou reach a hand out before you can stop yourself. As your skin touches the cold metal, you feel a rush of power.\r\n\r\nThe thrill of battle. The soaring heartbeat of a duel. The off-beat note of a parry.\r\n\r\nThe brutal satisfaction of sinking your blade into your enemy's flesh, that feeling both disgusting and triumphant.\r\n\r\nYour fingers tingle. Your vision is red. You have already grabbed your weapon, turning to fight the next enemy.\r\n\r\nAs you step away from the Shadowgraft, your vision returns to normal. Your breath returns and your heartbeat slows.\r\n\r\nYou know deep in your bones that this metal will make you braver and stronger.\r\n\r\nYou also know that if you are bound by it, you will never be yourself again.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Shadowgraft Harness",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 618571,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-203475"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Gyre, \r\n\r\nThere is an urgent mission that requires a seasoned champion of Stormwind such as yourself. \r\n\r\nQuickly, meet me behind Stormwind Keep, and tell no one!\r\n\r\n<The paper is not signed, only branded with with an insignia of SI:7.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Urgent Stormwind Summons",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 203475,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-579123"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "They believe its silent vigil kept the horrors of the rift at bay. But the flame dimmed and the horrors escaped. Eventually, the flame was moved to preserve it.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Words of Obayo--Part 1: The Flame",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579123,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-525293"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Gather as much lightwood as you are able. The elves will know we are here soon enough. We must arm ourselves before they do. See it done!\r\n\r\n--Zul'jan",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Amani Missive",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 525293,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579241"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Some feel the call, and hunt for the missing goddess. We have scoured every inch of Harandar, as our traditions allow.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "Some seek the goddess far beyond Harandar. The elders do not approve, but when they hear the call, all they can do is seek. Though it is almost unheard of in the past centuries, legends claim that in ancient time enough haranir left that they could have formed new tribes. We are, after all, hunters. But none have found her, and where could you hide a goddess?",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Seeker's Trail--Part 3: Unending Mission",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579241,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-613887"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<A handwritten sheet of music intended for the lyre, only partially filled in. The thin paper is brittle with age.>\r\n\r\n\r\n\"Dawn's Caress\"\r\n\r\nDedicated to His Grace, Prince Kael'thas Sunstrider\r\n\r\n\r\nComposer - Lirath Windrunner",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Unfinished Sheet Music",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 613887,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-241470"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<HTML><BODY>\r\n<BR/><BR/>\r\n<H1 align=\"center\">General Lena Stormpike</H1>\r\n<IMG src=\"Interface\\Common\\spacer\" align=\"center\" width=\"1\" height=\"27\"/>\r\n<P>\r\nA stalwart combatant and defender of justice, fallen defending her home from the foul demons of the Burning Legion. Azeroth is darker for her passing.\r\n</P>\r\n</BODY></HTML>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "General Lena Stormpike",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 241470,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-180088"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "To my love,\r\n\r\nI confess that I remember. By some miracle, this echo of our past found me. I saved it, and with it, saved all that we were.\r\n\r\nPerhaps it was my undoing. I scorned the Archon's trust and so fell prey to this nightmare.\r\n\r\nBut the flicker of you comforts me in my final moments. Fate is blind to this horizon, but may we be as one anew.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Handwritten Note",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 180088,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["Item-191733"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Malygos, my Aspect...\r\n\r\nThe dracthyr remain securely in stasis, and my long vigil watching over them continues. While I am reluctant to trouble you, I fear I must report that the integrity of this creche has been compromised.\r\n\r\nAn insectoid infestation has breached these halls. In my own arrogance, I at first believed this incursion would prove little more than an annoyance of unwanted pests.\r\n\r\nBut now the contamination spreads out of control, and I find myself short of breath as I am overwhelmed by the toxins produced by this invasive species.\r\n\r\nI refuse to abandon the post you assigned to me, but I must request additional aid. It seems my arcane skills are insufficient to counteract this malady.\r\n\r\nYour loyal servant,\r\n\r\nAndesigos",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Report: Infestation",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 191733,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-252302"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Good news, everyone! No one will ever find my masterpiece!\r\n\r\nStitchwork is nearly complete. Just a few more pieces and some elbow grease, perhaps some ooze and/or gas...\r\n\r\nSuch imbeciles! They never think to look for trap doors in my lab. Well, there was that one adventurer, but now she's part of Stitchwork.\r\n\r\nNow, where did I leave my... Oh, delightful! Why am I still writing this down?",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Professor Putricide's Lost Journal",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 252302,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-553910"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Netherstrand Longbow\r\n\r\nThere are some who claim the Netherstrand Longbow was first carried by the Highborne in the War of the Ancients. Others say that it was not forged until Kael'thas journeyed to Outland and saw the expanse of the Twisting Nether with his own eyes.\r\n\r\nWhat is known is that strands of magic drawn from the Twisting Nether itself make the Netherstrand one of the deadliest bows ever used. The longbow was recovered from Outland after the forces of Kael'thas used it against the draenei. Perhaps its damaged legacy can be purified in the light of the Sunwell.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Netherstrand Longbow",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 553910,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-618542"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<This regal domanaar armor sits in a heavy silence. Despite its expert make, an aura of malice warps the breastplate's perfection. It is displayed alongside the following inscription.>\r\n\r\nVaras, whose greatest delight was martial prowess, raised Obscurion Citadel from nothing. He donned the impenetrable Lorica Umbra in battle. It turned away every blade or spell that sought to harm its wearer.\r\n\r\nWhen the Devouring Host demanded he surrender, Varas refused. With his armor, he could not be defeated.\r\n\r\nBut then, Xal'atath came to Varas alone. She whispered words into his ear that are known only between them. After a pause, Varas removed the Lorica Umbra. Then, at Xal'atath's command, he was killed.\r\n\r\nShe is the Void. Think to stand above her, this fate too shall be yours.\r\n\r\n-Lord Terminas\r\n\r\n<The Lorica Umbra has no chance of fitting you.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Void Armor",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 618542,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-507966"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<Much of this text has been worn away over the years, or made illegible with bloodstains. A bookmarked passage stands out to you.>\r\n\r\nMy Blessed Lord has gifted me with renewed life, and a new citadel from which I have been tasked the honor of overseeing a branch of his army. I, who attempted to betray him... have been rewarded. \r\n\r\nPerhaps I should have focused my studies on the curiosities of necromancy. After all, what use is the Sunwell's power if one has passed beyond the realm of the living? \r\n\r\nI am eternal, now. And I have Arthas to thank for it.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Profane Research",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 507966,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579244"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Although the fungarians often fear us, they will speak to us. This does not make it easier to learn from them. They answer with little thought and always have questions of their own. So many questions.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tending the Lands--Part 3: The Cycle",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579244,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-572447"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "One of a thousand broken spears littering the Hellfire Ramparts. Whether it belonged to a Horde or Alliance soldier is unclear--time cares little for such distinctions.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Scarred Spear",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 572447,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-140263"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "THE EMERALD ASCENSION\r\n\r\nFear not the time when great Sargeras's shadow eclipses the sun. \r\n\r\nThat is the moment of our ascension. \r\n\r\nDeath will follow, but it is only a doorway. \r\n\r\nStep through, and you will shed your frail skin and take on a form kissed by emerald fire.\r\n\r\nDig the ash from your eyes, and you will find a higher purpose at Sargeras's side.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Worn Pamphlet",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 140263,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-613850"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "...and while they may be mighty and regal, it is important to remember that hawkstriders are, above all else, highly nervous creatures. They must be allowed at least one hour of uninterrupted preening time per day in order to relieve stress. \r\n\r\nIt is recommended to separate hawkstriders during preening time. Do not attempt to help your hawkstrider preen, and do not permit your hawkstrider to preen you. Both can be considered displays of...\r\n\r\n<The book continues like this for several hundred pages.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Hawkstrider Husbandry: Unabridged Edition",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 613850,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-57756"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<The letter is missing entries as the ink has washed away in many places.>\r\n\r\n... every form of ... has been based ... on the antagonism of oppressing and oppressed ...\r\n\r\n... nothing to lose, but your chains ...\r\n\r\n... the past cannot be forgotten ...\r\n\r\n... cannot be forgiven ...\r\n\r\n... will RISE AGAIN!\r\n\r\n\r\n",
},
},
},
