["GameObject-620325"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<This set of tablets is old and weathered but seems like it has been well taken care of. However, only parts of them are legible.>\r\n\r\nPraise Akil'zon, whose covenant with our ruling family ensures our victory endures.\r\n\r\nPraise Jan'alai that our line of leaders through birth and death continues forever.\r\n\r\nPraise Halazzi for the clever Witherbark scribes who keep our records.\r\n\r\nPraise Nalorakk that these tablets, their archive, and our home that holds them never falls.\r\n\r\nAnd most of all praise ZUL'JIN who commissioned these tablets to renew our records and preserve our history that has been lost.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE SLOPES OF ZANDALAR\r\n\r\nCountless ages of our history have been lost either due to loss of elders keeping our oral traditions, or disasters and war.\r\n\r\nWhat is written here has been researched by Witherbark scholars and scribes commissioned by our warlord, ZUL'JIN.\r\n\r\nIN THE BEGINNING, the five (the Amani, the Witherbark, the Revantusk, the Shadowpine, and even the Vilebranch) tribes were one: THE AMANI--one family. And at the head was our patriarch MANZAJIN. He fought against the Zandalari, their greed, and their subjugation, to carve out borders of a new, free land.\r\n\r\nThe Amani continued for centuries in stability despite the Zandalari refusing to recognize the authority of the Amani tribe.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE MIGRATION\r\n\r\nThe names of MANZAJIN'S descendents have been lost, but what we do know is this: they pledged to rid the northeast of Kith'ix and the aqir and our bonds to the Zandalari.\r\n\r\nAs they traveled, they found their ability to call upon the loa weakened by the distance from their lands and the meddling of Kith'ix.\r\n\r\nEven so, their armies dispatched Kith'ix. The Amani cleansed the aqir from the land and created the vast Atal'Utek as a monument to their great battle but forbade entrance to its temple. \r\n\r\nWith this great victory began the AMANI EMPIRE OF ZUL'AMAN!",
},
{
["Page"] = 4,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE LOA OF ZUL'AMAN\r\n\r\nIt was in this time that the Amani became known to the loa of Zul'Aman and they to us. At first, we worshipped many, some worshipping still the loa of the Zandalari like Shadra and Hir'eek but, due to the distance, not often not receiving their blessing. Others worshipped minor loa.\r\n\r\nBut soon from the line of Zul'jin came the first Amani leader with the title hash'ey, Kindo'jan. Kindo'jan received the blessing of the four most powerful loa of Zul'Aman--Akil'zon, Halazzi, Jan'alai, and Nalorakk, and thus also the minor loa in the region.\r\n\r\nHe was so beloved of Akil'zon that from then on, the loa became not only the Loa of VICTORY but also the Loa of the Amani tribe and its leaders.\r\n\r\nKindo'jan commissioned the temple city of Atal'Aman and the temples Akil'alor, Jan'alor, Halaz'alor, and Nal'alor.",
},
{
["Page"] = 5,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE HASH'EY\r\n\r\nKindo'jan the hash'ey lived a long life spanning many generations. He established the order of the Loa Speakers and formalized the worshipful rituals we use still. Families began to group together near the temples of the loa that they worshipped most.\r\n\r\nThe Amani ruling family and others that worshipped Akil'zon settled in the temple city Atal'Aman and Amani'Zar.\r\n\r\nThe Witherbark settled in the region known as the Witherbark Bluffs.\r\n\r\nThe Shadowpine settled near Jan'alor and the islands around it, moving with the seasons.\r\n\r\nThe Revantusk settled near Nalorakk's Prowl.\r\n\r\nAnd the Vilebranch settled near Maisara, still clinging to the loa of the old lands.\r\n\r\nDespite living a long life, the hash'ey left no direct descendants, and encouraged his people to choose their next leader for their strength in mind, body, and spirit.",
},
{
["Page"] = 6,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: ATAI'NATHA\r\n\r\nDespite his wish, perhaps due to their love of Kindo'jan, ATAI'NATHA, distant relative of Kindo'jan from a colony near Zandalar, assumed the throne. He was conceited and vain in his appearance. He wore his scarlet hair long and had his tusks capped with gold and gems, in the style of the Zandalari.\r\n\r\nHe worshipped the loa, but they had no love for him. Akil'zon liked not the look in his eye, Halazzi the deception in his voice, Nalorakk his strange smell, and Jan'alai the darkness in his heart.\r\n\r\nThey were right to not trust him. He had a claw of precious gems and gold to wear made for him, but in secret, he had Vilebranch crafters use old, dark magic to give it power.\r\n\r\nWith it, he ruthlessly expanded Zul'Aman's borders, but also would use his claw to kill anyone who dissented. In the end, he was poisoned by his own servants at the urging of the chieftains of the other Amani tribes. \r\n\r\nHis claw was destroyed and so ended his life and rule.",
},
{
["Page"] = 7,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: REVANTUSK RISING\r\n\r\nThe death of Atai'natha left the Amani in disarray unril NOROBU THE SCARRED, general of the Amani and leader of the Revantusk, stepped forward to be tested--and won. After days of feasting and deliberating, Norobu was made leader.\r\n\r\nNorobu created a council consisting of the chief of each tribe and bade them to meet at Amani'Zar. \r\n\r\nDevout of Nalorakk, he knew war would come, but in the time between, decreed that the Amani fortify themselves.\r\n\r\nHe fortified Atal'Aman with stone, built walls, and commissioned the Throne of Manzajin: a place where the council could meet but also engage in sport, feasting, and celebration.\r\n\r\nNorobu, who held no ill will towards Atai'natha after his death, adopted his children, who revered him and never sought the throne.\r\n\r\nNorobu ushered in a new tradition of only the worthy of spirit, mind, and body ruling Zul'Aman.",
},
{
["Page"] = 8,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: BEFORE THE SUNDERING\r\n\r\nTheir names are lost, but based on ancient carvings, after Norobu's death, the duty of chieftain shifted from tribe to tribe, and our tribes--the Revantusk and the Witherbark--reached out in trade to other troll nations, establishing settlements of their own.\r\n\r\nLong after we settled away from Zandalar, we found war again--this time against our most hated foe: the elves. Before what the gokinye call \"The Sundering,\" the Pale Queen's empire spread far to the east, encroaching on our lands. Despite our skirmishes with them and mutual hatred, the Zandalari kings and Azshara struck a bargain, ceding land to them to end hostilities.\r\n\r\nWe saw this not as \"shrewd diplomacy,\" but as weakness.\r\n\r\nWhen the earth cracked, we thought the raging sea would keep the elves away, but they returned. They sacked the sacred burial site of our hash'ey, the markets of Tor'Yunta, and with magic created a new city--Silvermoon.\r\n\r\nOur hatred began anew.",
},
{
["Page"] = 9,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THALASSIAN WAR\r\n\r\nThe destruction of Tor'Yunta and the loss of Atal'Kindo caused us a great distress and sparked wars over years without number.\r\n\r\nFinally, Chieftain Tan'dani, a cunning strategist of the Witherbark tribe, led our forces into battle, slowly gaining ground in guerilla attacks but also suffering heavy losses.\r\n\r\nIt was then the Zandalari, from over the waters, offered us aid. They would help us regain our territory with nothing in return but good will.\r\n\r\nTan'dari saw through their offer. She knew that with their help came the eventual vassalage of the Amani Empire.\r\n\r\nBut during a diplomatic journey to meet with the Zandalari ambassadors, she disappeared. The Zandalari, with their belief in castes and hereditary rule, put a young but fierce Amani of royal blood--able to trace his line to Manzajin--on the throne.\r\n\r\nThus began the rule of JINTHA.",
},
{
["Page"] = 10,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: BATTLE FOR ATAL'KINDO\r\n\r\nWith JINTHA, heir of the Amani, back on the throne, the Amani set to scour the elven city conjured from air and the well from our lands. A combined army of both humans and elves poised to attack on different flanks.\r\n\r\nThinking the humans easy prey, Jintha attacked the humans on his southern flank, but fell into a trap made by the humans and elves there.\r\n\r\nJintha perished in the flames produced by the human mages. Seeing this, the Zandalari abandoned the fight and the Amani were forced to retreat behind the current boundary of Zul'Aman.\r\n\r\nIt is unclear who took over from Jintha as ruler, but it seems as though the role passed from the tribe again.\r\n\r\nFinally, ZUL'JIN of the AMANI was tested and began a new age.",
},
{
["Page"] = 11,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE REIGN OF ZUL'JIN\r\n\r\nThe reign of WARLORD ZUL'JIN marked a new beginning for our people ushering in an era of pride in our culture and a return as a world power.\r\n\r\nZul'jin reunited the tribes of the Witherbark, Revantusk, Shadowpine, and Vilebranch as one Amani.\r\n\r\nHe fought valiantly against the elves, keeping them off balance and away from Zul'Aman, always looking for a way to rid them from our lands for good.\r\n\r\nAfter being captured and rescued by the Horde, he allied with them in return for restoring our homeland.\r\n\r\nBut the Horde abandoned the fight and Zul'jin's army was pushed back by the elves in Doomhammer's War.\r\n\r\nYayo'jin the Mystic prophesied Zul'jin would harness a power greater than anyone had ever known and that the time of a new hash'ey was near.\r\n\r\nKnowing now that he can trust no one but his Amani, his advisor, Malacrass, wise hexpriest of the Vilebranch, has promised to help him secure the power to reclaim what's ours.",
},
{
["Page"] = 12,
["Text"] = "<It is clear that the etching on the top of the tablet has been ground down, and a sorrowful carving of a funeral procession has been carved on top of it. Based on the letters you can still discern underneath, you can tell this tablet was supposed to be on the continuation of Zul'jin's reign--not his death.>\r\n\r\nTHE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE DEATH OF ZUL'JIN\r\n\r\nOn the eve of obtaining the power to conquer the elves and return our lands, we were beset by an army of gokinye who invaded our temple city of Atal'Aman.\r\n\r\nOur warlord has died. Malacrass's body has not been recovered, and his only heir, Man'ye, the Aspect of Akil'zon, has died as well.\r\n\r\nWe know not what transpired within Atal'Aman. All that fought there are dead. Even the loa are silent in our defeat either in sorrow, anger, or shame.\r\n\r\nYoung ZUL'JARRA, Man'ye's daughter, already shows great promise. ZARAMA, her mother, will reign until she can be tested.\r\n\r\nLong live ZUL'JARRA long live ZARAMA.",
},
{
["Page"] = 13,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: \r\n\r\n<Much of the top of this tablet's text has been obliterated and recarved in a threatening motif of warriors with their tusks bared and their eyes wide.\r\n\r\nHowever, you can make out two chieftain entries. You believe the names are likely KAZRA'JIN and DAAKARA. You can also make out something referencing the name Zul.>\r\n\r\nDuring the turmoil that was beget by Zul'jin's death, the tribe fractured, some wanting to claim the power Zul'jin sought, others later to conquer abroad with the help of the Zandalari. They led many, but had selfish aims.\r\n\r\nThey were laid low by fate. Let no one mourn them! And let no one cross our borders under pain of death!",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "The Rulers of Zul'Aman",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 620325,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-180516"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "You have discovered the location of the shrine!  Upon further examination, you sense a stronger pulse of the strange power that has gripped the Isle.  You feel a bit uncomfortable standing by the shrine... and perhaps a little disturbed.\r\n\r\nThe bronze placard along the side of the shrine reads:\r\n\r\n\"Here stands the Shrine of Dath'Remar, a fitting tribute to a noble elf.  Let all who gaze on this monument remember his sacrifices for our people and his dedication to the cause of our continued survival.  All who prosper in Quel'Thalas do so thanks to him.\"",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Shrine of Dath'Remar",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 180516,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-557910"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<HTML><BODY>\r\n<H1 align=\"center\">Aln'hara's Bloom</H1>\r\n<HR/>\r\n<P>\r\nA woven vessel of vine and bark cradles a single radiant flower. Its petals shimmer with a soft, living glow. When held close, a faint hum like distant singing can be heard.\r\n<BR/><BR/>\r\nIt is said this bloom carries an echo of the goddess--a piece of the song that first called the haranir to Harandar.\r\n</P>\r\n</BODY></HTML>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Aln'hara's Bloom",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 557910,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-252385"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "I am Illysanna, daughter of the resistance commander Kur'talos Ravencrest. You should know by now that my father is dead. I am not the only one who has lost someone. Our great empire, our entire world, is burning before our eyes.\r\n\r\nNothing in this war with the Burning Legion has gone according to plan. Nothing. Every battle we win is followed by two defeats. Every demon we slay is replaced by ten more.\r\n\r\nLike my father, I was once so certain of victory. So overconfident. So foolish. Most resistance fighters still are. They hold tight to their archaic ways, unwilling to accept that we cannot best our enemy through conventional means. We are fighting something alien to this world, something born of nightmare.\r\n\r\nThere is one elf who understands this: Illidan Stormrage. He knows that to defeat the demons, we must adapt. We must embrace extraordinary new tactics. If not, we will die. It is as simple as that.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "Perhaps you consider Illidan an arrogant sorcerer, or even a menace to our way of life. I once did, but my opinions have changed. I am writing to explain why, and to chronicle what I have learned of Illidan. Despite his dangerous reputation, I believe he is our only chance of surviving the days ahead.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Torn Page",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 252385,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579238"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "I have ignored the risks. When I was in the painting of a battle, some dark creature lashed out. I am still fevered from its venom.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "These are no mere visions, and they're more than memories. Ribs are broken, and the venom nearly reached my heart. But the rewards seem worth the price.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "I must share my secrets, and train the next generation to be wiser than I was. Create, learn, and share--but temper and be aware. Each image can bring ruin. Each memory can bring death. And the Alndust is too precious to waste. Only a few will carry this honor, to let others live our past.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Echoes of Our Past--Part 3: Dangerous Memories",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579238,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-290682"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "HERE LIE -\r\nKing Rahu'ai and his trusted advisors, Atu and M'bara. Long did he rule. Painful was his fall.",
},
},
},
