[266846] = {
["BroadcastText"] = {
["enUS"] = {
["When the elders had agreed, a few select chosen would journey north to the highest peak in the land to make the offerings."] = true,
["As a farewell to An'she in the cooler seasons, these neighboring tribes would celebrate one last sun blossom ceremony."] = true,
["Retracing the path of this great summer migration reminds us that even as the light of the sun wanes and the days grow shorter, our path home will always be illuminated by the fires of An'she."] = true,
["Sun blossoms drift high in the skies above. Set them aflame as tribute to An'she!"] = true,
["Long ago, before the Sun Blossom ritual was practiced, the tauren tribes would journey to Stonetalon to celebrate Midsummer."] = true,
["As the cooler winds descended upon Thousand Needles, the tribes here gathered atop the southern bluffs to ignite their blossoms."] = true,
["Although the sands of Tanaris are now an arid wasteland, these once-lush lands were home to many tauren tribes."] = true,
["Cenarius advised them to seek the mistress of the skies atop the great mountain, as they would need her boon to bring their offerings into the skies."] = true,
["As the tribes ventured south, some followed the rocky ridges that divided the plains of Mashan'she and the rolling valleys of Mulgore."] = true,
["As the sun pilgrims traversed the rivers south, they wondered: had it truly been the offerings of the Blossoms themselves that had appeased An'she..."] = true,
["As some tribes traversed the jungles, others kept to the steppes and cliffs that divided their territories."] = true,
["Some tribes returned home to the plains of Mashan'she, as others broke off toward the jungles of Feralas."] = true,
["Some say these tribes were the first to make the pilgrimage north, following the path of the great beasts migrating to cooler pastures."] = true,
["Aviana was a goddess of winds and wild, and this was not a land the tauren usually ventured to."] = true,
["It is said that as the pilgrims descended the waterways into the red forests below, the blaze of An'she seemed to dissipate."] = true,
["These bonfires would serve as path markers for the southern tribes as they made their way home during the end of Midsummer."] = true,
["Cenarius saw wisdom in the tauren reaching out to An'she, and granted them shelter and the cool waters of his glade as respite."] = true,
["An'she was now sated and the tauren tribes agreed to carry out this ritual journey at the start of every Midsummer."] = true,
["\"The shu'halo rarely risk journeying so high up these slopes, yet I see the selflessness of your purpose. May these winds carry your blossoms high above.\""] = true,
["These plains would serve as a rest stop and hunting grounds for many tribes of central Kalimdor, long before Thunderbluff ever stood."] = true,
["These tribes paid homage to both wind and fire with their celebration."] = true,
["Yet, as the tauren pressed on, they found even the cold alpine forests of Winterspring had felt the blaze of the sun overhead."] = true,
["As the Summer pilgrims continued further into kaldorei lands, they stopped to rest in the once green Irontree Woods."] = true,
["Although the kaldorei and tauren kept an amicable distance, the elven priestesses granted our request and guided us through their lands."] = true,
["There, the ancients of the forests welcomed them with shade and shelter from the scorching heat."] = true,
["As the southern tribes traveled, flame keepers would build great bonfires to maintain the light of An'she during the colder nights."] = true,
["When ignited, sun blossoms would soar upwards in the warm summer winds. But with the sun high in the sky, the blossoms would not reach."] = true,
["But such a journey involved entering the moonlit lands of the kaldorei..."] = true,
["\"Perhaps we should offer them from the highest mountain?\" another suggested."] = true,
["During one particularly hot summer, as the sun blazed and the crops wilted, the elders pondered on how to appease An'she."] = true,
["Our first resting point was at the shrine of the Wisp Mother. Here, we shared our stories of An'she with the kaldorei."] = true,
["The pilgrimage continued with a detour into the grove of Moonglade, home of Cenarius the Forest Lord."] = true,
["This retreat, often known as the Brow of the Sun, served as the final resting point for the tribes who made their home in Thousand Needles."] = true,
["\"Perhaps a bundle of sun blossoms will appease him?\" one suggested. An offering to the Sun was needed."] = true,
},
},
