["enUS"] = "Ley-Keeper Velania",
},
},
[252528] = {
["BroadcastText"] = {
["enUS"] = {
["Even so, after breaking free from the Firelord's chains, the Dark Iron clan have once again embraced their faith in the flame and reverence for the element that flows through their veins."] = true,
["The Summer Festival of Fire has long been a time of revel and good fortune for the Kingdom of Stormwind."] = true,
["Inspired by their neighbor's celebration, the people of Brightwood would soon set ablaze their own blossom lights and rekindled their region's festival."] = true,
["Although humanity's celebration of summer predates even the kingdom of Strom, it was their kinship with the dwarves that inspired many customs still practiced today."] = true,
["The story tells of the first wildsages witnessing a brilliant burning streak shooting across the summer night sky."] = true,
["Following the star as it illuminated the crags and foothills of Khaz Modan, the wildsages watched from afar as it briefly settled over the second highest mountain in the land."] = true,
["The blossom lights drift above on a summer breeze. Set them ablaze and honor the fire festival!"] = true,
["Around the bonfire, the Arathi elders spoke of the dwarves' star, and how this elemental spirit and others like it made its home in the untamed valley to the north."] = true,
["In later seasons, the people of Westfall and Elwynn joined their neighbors in reigniting the festival."] = true,
["With most of northern Redridge and its resource rich territories lost, paranoia and fear set in around Stormwind and soon, many celebrations fell out of practice."] = true,
["Unbeknownst to the humans, the Thane of the Dark Iron dwarves, Thaurissan the First, had called forth the Firelord from his elemental banishment, blanketing the realm in ash and soot."] = true,
["They say the summer winds carried these lights into the haunted canyon of Deadwind Pass, bringing a flicker of hope to the kingdom's darkest places."] = true,
["Long ago, at the height of midsummer celebrations, the northern mountains of Redridge were shattered by a catastrophic eruption."] = true,
["But what was once a season of celebration, became a chapter of paranoia and darkness for the people in these lands."] = true,
["For the Dark Irons, a weapon to wield and master. And for the Wildhammer, the flicker of flame was our tool for survival in the rugged mountains of Khaz Modan."] = true,
["Above them, on emberlit wings, circling high above the tallest peak of the land, the wildsages saw their star, like a glittering torch in the summer sky."] = true,
["Much like Lake Everstill, the rivers of these regions were dotted with blossom lights and in time, the once abandoned festival returned to all corners of the Kingdom."] = true,
["One such tale told of the origins of the Wildsage Pilgrimage, carried out at the end of each summer, in the wake of a fiery shooting star."] = true,
["It is said that the pilgrims even witnessed the great star dancing among the thunder strikes atop the northern-most mountain in these highlands."] = true,
["Having already established trade with Khaz Modan, the ancient humans were quick to welcome the exhausted pilgrims into their Midsummer celebrations."] = true,
["As the star swept northwest across the sea, the wildsages crossed the narrow channel into the human lands, where they found another celebration underway."] = true,
["Marked forever as an important natural landmark for the wildsage yearly pilgrimage, this mountain would later house the great Wildhammer fortress of Grim Batol."] = true,
["Continuing their journey, the wildsages passed into the valley, where they set their eyes upon majestic winged creatures soaring high in the sky."] = true,
["Believing it as an auspicious sign from the spirits of fire, they followed it, climbing high into the mountains of Dun Morogh, where they saw it dart to the northeast."] = true,
["It is said that while many descendants of King Thoradin migrated south by sea, those who traveled by land were guided through Khaz Modan by Wildhammer bonfires during the dwarven festivals of fire."] = true,
["Though the dwarven festivals of fire were celebrated by all clans in the ages before the War of Three Hammers, the Dark Iron clan paid a heavy toll for summoning the Firelord."] = true,
["In fact, since the dawn of dwarven kind, fire has played a crucial role in the shaping and forging of our people. For the Bronzebeards, a tool of industry and trade."] = true,
["As the wildsages learned the maypole dances, and the dwarves taught the Arathi how to weave blossom lights, both races shared in their stories and customs under the warm summer skies."] = true,
["Through great tenacity, the people of Lakeshire were the first to rebuild and rekindled the summer celebration, choosing to honor the spirit of fire, not fear it."] = true,
["As the Wildhammer hosted the festival in their foothills, the wisest and eldest of their shamans, known to some as \"wildsages\", would tell stories around the bonfires."] = true,
["The wildsages followed the star over rolling hills and vast river lands under open skies; a journey through lands rich with elemental spirits--another auspicious sign."] = true,
},
